      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Translation refresh (watcher)",
      "summary": "Keep every locale current after the source moves: detect, refresh the templates, merge them into each locale, translate only what is new or fuzzy, check it, and land one PR per instance on main.",
      "description": "Keep every locale current after the source moves: detect, refresh the templates, merge them into each locale, translate only what is new or fuzzy, check it, and land one PR per instance on main.\n\nYou are in this process when the watcher scheduled by `multi-locale-translation` wakes, or when a template check has failed. It is the loop that process ends with. A fresh session can run it cold: the skill `translation-refresh` gives each step as a command, and each instance's own AGENTS.md names what is particular to it. One run walks every instance in turn, and each instance with something to refresh gets its own PR.\n\nA refresh never re-translates a finished string. Obsolete strings are kept as `#~` entries, new ones arrive empty, and only new and fuzzy strings are translated, with the terms the term base already fixes. The round trip runs on the changed strings only.",
      "enforcement": "advisory",
      "sourcePath": "library/processes/translation-refresh.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/library/processes/translation-refresh.bpmn",
